The attached image (Figure 4) displays confocal microscopy data illustrating the uptake of antigen and Nano-11 by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). The top row shows Nano-11 (red) uptake, while the middle row indicates minimal uptake of soluble FITC-labeled ovalbumin (OVA, green). The bottom row demonstrates a significantly enhanced uptake of OVA (green) by BMDCs when complexed with Nano-11 (red). The merged images confirm the colocalization of Nano-11 and OVA within the cells, providing visual evidence that Nano-11 effectively delivers adsorbed protein antigens into dendritic cells, a crucial mechanism for initiating an immune response.